:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=SRJ.Submit Restore Journal
:P.This command was created to allow quick restoring of journals in a
batch program. It requires that EXPJRNE exists in library TK. EXPJRNE
is an open source project you can google it needed.
:P.This command just submits a call the EXPJRNE command to restore journal
entries to a specified file.
:P.To use, enter the command followed by the file name you want the journals
for an press enter. Including the file first allows the program to populate
a lot of the other parameters.
:P.By default the the program will restore the last 5 days worth of journal
entries to a file that is the same as the original file name with RJ appended
to it. The file willbe created in a librarty that is the same as the user
profiel running the command. All the defaults are overridable when the
command is prompted.
:H2.Example:
:P.RJS FLPOHDR <f4>
:P.This opens the command prompt with the defaults filled in to
restore the journals for file FLPOHDR for the last 5 days to file
FLPOHDRRJ in a library the same as the user prompting the command.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SRJ/OBJ'.Object - File to Restore Journals For
:XH3.Object - File to Restore Journals For
:P.This field allows entry of the file name to restore journals for. It
is qualified the a file and library name can be entered.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SRJ/OBJTYPE'.OBJTYPE - Object Type
:XH3.OBJTYPE - Object Type
:P.This parameter allows the object type to be entered. It defaults
to *FILE since the intent of this program is to restore journals for a
file. It can be changed to any object type the EXPJRNE command supports.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SRJ/FROMDATE'.FROMDATE - From Date
:XH3.FROMDATE - From Date
:P.This is the date to restore journals back to. It can be a date in the
system date format or a number of days. If a number of days is used,
it will calculate the date for that many days prior to the current date.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SRJ/OUTFILE'.OUTFILE - Output File
:XH3.OUTFILE - Output File
:P.Specifies the name of the output file to restreo the journals
to. This will overlay the file if it already exists. It is best
to restore the journals to developement library where they will
not get in the way.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SRJ/JOBNAME'.JOBNAME - Job Name
:XH3.JOBNAME - Job Name
:P.Specifies the name of the job used on the SBMJOB command. This
can be useful to see if the job is still running.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:EPNLGRP.
